], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1473, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1473, "cached_input": 63284, "input": 64759, "output": 213}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 81285, "other": 423, "system": 34618, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 61168}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 191891}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "8c10c597-e203-5eb1-8191-cdc56cd3c172", "at": 1795658837.6370625, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 136484, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "6d9ab35f2d17684aa3c70a8011f988ef", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "04eea004-e4d2-5e09-9081-d8dfa936f831", "at": 1795658837.649974, "until": 1795658839.6428642, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 136485, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "6d9ab35f2d17684aa3c70a8011f988ef", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_014oiUcbN7MyQZNQPbDarno2", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/storywiki && git remote set-url origin \"${HT_FORGEJO_URL%/}$(git remote get-url origin | sed -E 's#^https?://[^/]+##')\"; timeout 90 git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 1946051 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | grep…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/storywiki && git remote set-url origin \"${HT_FORGEJO_URL%/}$(git remote get-url origin | sed -E 's#^https?://[^/]+##')\"; timeout 90 git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 1946051 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | grep -i \"rev. 2[0-9]\\|rev 2[0-9]\\|P6\" | cut -c1-1800 | head"]], "output": "```console\n88410df Outline rev 20: record what the paper already says\n69adc08 Outline rev 20: Holme-Kim check, tail-and-clustering reading dropped (Brief rev 17)\n1946051 Outline rev 19: P7 'consistent with', Holme-Kim check weak support (Brief rev 16)\n+- **Rev. 20 record (Brief rev. 17).** Holme–Kim check: HK behaves like BA, so the two-factor (tail + clustering) reading gains no support and is dropped as an explanation; the cause of the real-graph (d) behaviour stays open, with exposure spread named only as a description (Spearman −0.95 at d=20, +0.21 at d=80, 9 graphs, not a test). The (b) form s(HM/AM−1) predicts the realised bias on HK and LN without refitting (HK −0.141/−0.163/−0.129 vs −0.147/−0.164/−0.127; LN −0.311/−0.278/−0.305 vs −0.314/−0.274/−0.311 at d=20/5/80); \"falls with d\" does not hold for HK or LN, as the near-Poisson condition says. Checked against `paper-repo` `dev` 8e015dd: §5.2 already claims no two-factor reading (tail alone and clustering alone do not reproduce it; the spread is a description), the Discussion only says thinning also changes clustering and the tail, and the appendix P7 paragraph says the block does not test the account and S_adj is not cited as evidence. One sentence is owed when the HK table is delivered: HK behaves like BA, so the tail-plus-clustering reading is not supported.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "4ad6c3a8-df26-5260-99f3-2f734f6cc8f3", "at": 1795658838.862289, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 136498, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "6d9ab35f2d17684aa3c70a8011f988ef", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "1b570a22-2d79-591c-8021-c43089b3f858", "at": 1795658838.8724265, "clock": "host", "stream": "runn